{
    "background_story": "Samuel was a charismatic cult leader who rose to power in the 1970s. He preached a message of spiritual enlightenment and self-discovery, but beneath the surface, he fostered a culture of idolatry. His followers, entranced by his charm and conviction, began to worship him as a messianic figure. Samuel encouraged this adoration, using it to manipulate and control those around him. He claimed to possess divine insight, and his devotees believed him, surrendering their autonomy and critical thinking. As the cult grew, so did Samuel's ego and desire for power. He became increasingly isolated and tyrannical, using his influence to exploit and harm those who questioned his authority. The cult eventually imploded, but not before leaving a trail of devastation and shattered lives in its wake. Samuel's legacy served as a cautionary tale about the dangers of unchecked power and the destructive nature of idolatry.",
